# TEMPLATE -- copy to argocd-notifications.sops.yaml, fill in, then:
#     task secrets:seal -- platform/secrets/argocd-notifications.sops.yaml
#
# The GitHub token Argo CD Notifications uses to report a failed sync or a
# Degraded Application to GitHub as a `repository_dispatch` (event type
# `argo-degraded`), which runs .github/workflows/auto-rollback.yaml.
#
# Create it at GitHub -> Settings -> Developer settings -> Fine-grained tokens:
#   Resource owner     ned-si
#   Repository access  Only select repositories: ned-si/homelab
#   Permissions        Contents: Read and write
#                      Pull requests: Read and write
#                      Issues: Read and write
#                      (Metadata: Read-only is added automatically)
# The same token is the repository Actions secret AUTO_ROLLBACK_TOKEN: the
# workflow opens the revert pull request, enables auto-merge and opens the
# issue with it (GitHub Actions may not open pull requests with its own token
# here, and a pull request opened by that token would not start CI).
#
# HOW IT IS CONSUMED
#
# bootstrap/argocd-values.yaml sets `notifications.secret.name` to this
# Secret's name, so the notifications controller reads it instead of the
# chart's argocd-notifications-secret, and the webhook service
# `github-dispatch` sends `Authorization: Bearer $github-token`. The
# controller watches the Secret: a new value applies without a restart.
#
# Sealed with a PENDING sentinel until the token exists: GitHub answers 401,
# nothing is dispatched, and automatic rollback stays off.
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: argocd-notifications-github
  namespace: argo
type: Opaque
stringData:
  github-token: PUT_THE_AUTO_ROLLBACK_GITHUB_TOKEN_HERE
